+Prefilled Operator Runbook — FalconAV (example vehicle)
+
+Purpose
+- Exact commands, env vars, thresholds and acceptance criteria to run hardware proofs, HIL certification, perception scale runs, provenance gating and certifier submission for the FalconAV vehicle class. Replace placeholders with your actual hostnames, secrets and thresholds before running.
+
+Secrets / env required (set locally or in CI):
+- COSIGN_KMS_URI — KMS URI for cosign key (e.g., kms://projects/.../keys/cosign)
+- REKOR_SERVER — Rekor server URL (e.g., https://rekor.example)
+- S3_UPLOAD — evidence S3 prefix (e.g., s3://aegis-evidence/falconav/run-<id>/)
+- WATTTIME_API_KEY — WattTime API key for carbon
+- CERTIFIER_API_TOKEN — API token for certifier upload (optional)
+- NPU_RUNNERS — comma-separated NPU test runners (e.g., npu-1.example,npu-2.example)
+
+Representative hardware (example values — replace)
+- ECUs:
+  - falcon-ecu-01.example.com: can0
+  - falcon-ecu-02.example.com: can0
+- HIL rig host: falcon-hil.example.com
+- Builder hosts: falcon-builder-1,falcon-builder-2
+
+Prefilled thresholds (example — tune to vehicle)
+- p99 loop jitter threshold: 0.5 ms
+- safe-stop latency threshold: 50 ms
+- perception FN target in certified envelope: 1e-3
+
+Directory/out layout (example)
+- OUT=/tmp/falconav_run_<ts>
+- RT proofs: $OUT/rt_proofs/<ecu>_can0/rt_slo_proof.json
+- HIL cert: $OUT/hil_cert/...
+- Perception: $OUT/perception/...
+- Auditor bundle: $OUT/falconav_auditor_bundle.tar.gz
+
+Step 0 — Preflight (validate runners)
+1) On each self-hosted runner and builder, run:
+   sudo /bin/bash ops/infra/hardening/check_runner_hardening.sh
+   # If missing, bootstrap:
+   sudo COSIGN_VERSION=v1.15.0 REKOR_VERSION=v0.12.0 LABELS="role=builder,npu=true" ./ops/infra/hardening/provision_and_label_runners.sh
+2) Install vendor SDKs per vendor (adapt):
+   sudo VENDOR=inferentia ./ops/infra/hardening/install_vendor_sdks.sh
+
+Step 1 — Hardware RT proofs (per-ECU)
+1) Prepare targets file: ops/av/rt/rt_sweep_targets.json
+   [
+     {"host":"falcon-ecu-01.example.com","iface":"can0"},
+     {"host":"falcon-ecu-02.example.com","iface":"can0"}
+   ]
+2) Run sweep and sign:
+   OUT=/tmp/falconav_run_$(date +%s)
+   TARGETS="falcon-ecu-01.example.com:can0,falcon-ecu-02.example.com:can0" \
+     COSIGN_KMS_URI=$COSIGN_KMS_URI S3_UPLOAD=$S3_UPLOAD \
+     ./ops/validation/run_rt_sweep_and_sign.sh "$OUT/rt_proofs"
+3) Inspect proofs:
+   jq . $OUT/rt_proofs/*/rt_slo_proof.json
+4) Acceptance:
+   - Each proof: p99_ms <= 0.5 and safe_ms <= 50 (adjust)
+5) If fail:
+   python3 ops/validation/rt_remediation_agent.py --report <proof> --out <proof_dir>/remediation.json
+   Apply suggested remediation (CPU isolation, IRQ affinity, kernel tuning), then re-run.
+
+Step 2 — Exhaustive HIL campaigns & formal closure
+1) Create scenario runners list: ops/av/certification/falcon_scenarios.txt
+   one command per line for each HIL scenario runner.
+2) Run closure loop (stops for operator triage on failure):
+   COSIGN_KMS_URI=$COSIGN_KMS_URI ./ops/robotics/control/certified/run_exhaustive_hil_and_close_formal.sh \
+       --scenarios-file ops/av/certification/falcon_scenarios.txt \
+       --golden /opt/aegis/golden_trace.ndjson --out "$OUT/hil_cert" --cosign $COSIGN_KMS_URI --max-iter 5
+3) Acceptance:
+   - campaign_summary.json: all critical scenarios ran_ok == true and compare_ok == true
+   - Apalache: no unresolved safety counterexamples for specified invariants
+4) On success: signed HIL cert bundle will be created and optionally uploaded to S3.
+
+Step 3 — Perception long-tail: sim -> HIL -> retrain -> NPU validation
+1) Run the full pipeline:
+   ./ops/av/perception/scale/run_sim_hil_field_pipeline.sh --packs 50 --per-pack 200 --parallel 8 \
+      --out "$OUT/perception" --npu-runners "$NPU_RUNNERS" --cosign "$COSIGN_KMS_URI"
+2) Inspect adv dataset:
+   ls "$OUT/perception/adv_dataset"
+3) Retrain (if not auto-triggered):
+   python3 ops/av/perception/scale/auto_retrain_pipeline.py --dataset "$OUT/perception/adv_dataset/adv_data.ndjson" --out "$OUT/perception/retrain" --npu-runners "$NPU_RUNNERS" --cosign-key "$COSIGN_KMS_URI"
+4) Validate ONNX on each NPU runner:
+   For each runner in $NPU_RUNNERS:
+     ssh $runner "python3 ops/hw/validation/npu_inference_smoke.py $OUT/perception/retrain/*.onnx"
+5) Acceptance:
+   - FN_rate <= 1e-3 in certified envelope
+   - ONNX artifacts smoke-tested on all NPU runners and cosign-signed
+
+Step 4 — Builder hardening & provenance enforcement (staging -> prod)
+1) On all builders:
+   sudo ./ops/infra/hardening/provision_and_label_runners.sh LABELS="role=builder,npu=true"
+   sudo /bin/bash ops/infra/hardening/check_runner_hardening.sh
+2) Test provenance enforcer locally:
+   IMAGE_MANIFESTS=deploy.yaml REKOR_SERVER=$REKOR_SERVER python3 ops/ci/promotion_gate/enforce_builder_provenance.py
+3) Acceptance:
+   - Enforcement exits 0 only when all hardware-affecting images are cosign-signed and Rekor-registered.
+
+Step 5 — Carbon tuning and audited overrides
+1) Run monitor mode to collect stats (14 days recommended):
+   python3 ops/carbon/monitor_tune.py --duration-s 1209600 --interval-s 300 --region US-CA --out "$OUT/carbon_tune.json"
+2) Tune threshold (aim FP < 5%) and set AEGIS_CARBON_THRESHOLD CI secret
+3) Override workflow:
+   Platform Owner issues cosign-signed override:
+     python3 ops/carbon/override_signer.py --approval-id FALCON-OVR-001 --approved-by owner@example.com --scope '{"manifests":"deploy.yaml"}' --out /tmp/override.json
+     cosign verify /tmp/override.json
+4) Acceptance:
+   - Monitor FP rate acceptable; override artifact created & auditable
+
+Step 6 — Build auditor bundle & submit to certifier
+1) Produce evidence manifest & bundle:
+   python3 ops/certifier/evidence_manifest_generator.py --root . --out "$OUT/evidence_manifest.json" --vehicle FalconAV --s3-base "$S3_UPLOAD"
+   ./ops/certifier/one_click_auditor_bundle.sh --out "$OUT/falconav_auditor_bundle.tar.gz"
+2) Submit:
+   python3 ops/certifier/submit_and_track_findings.py --bundle "$OUT/falconav_auditor_bundle.tar.gz" --upload-url "<CERT_UPLOAD_URL>" --findings-url "<CERT_FINDINGS_URL>" --api-token "$CERTIFIER_API_TOKEN" --outdir "$OUT/certifier_findings"
+3) Acceptance:
+   - Certifier response: accepted OR findings list with remediation plan. All critical findings closed within agreed timeline.
+
+Incident triage & escalation
+- If critical failure (safe-stop miss, HIL critical failure), run:
+   ./ops/runbooks/incident_triage_playbook.md
+   Immediately notify: controls-lead@example.com, safety-officer@example.com, perception-lead@example.com, infra@example.com
+
+Recordkeeping & audit
+- All scripts invoke ops.sdk.evidence_sdk.record_manifest to keep machine-readable evidence records. Keep S3 evidence paths and signed bundles for auditor.
+
+End of runbook. Replace all placeholders before running.
